#X obj 60 40 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty cz4.i~\ and\ cz4~ 24 6 0 22 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X obj 60 76 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Casio\ CZ-1\ with\ CZ\ tones\ and\ SysEx 24 6 0 16 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X obj 60 120 cz4.i~ 1;
#X text 190 120 <- click it: the editor, f 64;
#X obj 60 160 dac~;
#X obj 60 206 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty cz4.i~ 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 234 cz4.i~ is the whole instrument in one object: cz4~ \, the editor \, the controller layer \, the Launchkey pads and display \, MIDI in and out. Put it in a patch \, connect the two left outlets to dac~ and play. Click it to open the editor \, see Editor. \; Argument 1 is the MIDI channel (0 or none = 1) \, argument 2 the channel of the pads (0 or none = 10 \, the Drums Channel). Several cz4.i~ do not get in each other's way \, each has its own editor. Page 1 of the controller is PERFORM \, page k is row k of the editor. \; cz4~ is the bare engine inside \, for patches of your own: inlet 2 takes the velocity of a note sent as a float \, inlet 3 raw MIDI bytes from midiin (notes with velocity \, bend \, aftertouch \, program change \, CC 1 \, 7 \, 64 and CZ SysEx) \, and the floats of outlet 3 (SysEx) go to midiout. Open cz4.i~ to see the wiring., f 64;
#X obj 60 488 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Editor 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 516 The editor is the window of cz4.i~. Every change shows up in it \, from the controller \, a tone change \, messages or SysEx. refresh asks for all values again. \; Rows of 8 below the TONE band \, titled as in Controls: row k is page k of the controller layer. Each cell: name and label \, a slider and a number box with the value as from a pot (0 to 127) \, the box beside it the value as the CZ shows it. Edits are heard at once. \; Line \, envelope and tone: the LINE / WAVE \, ENVELOPE \, RATES and LEVELS rows edit the line chosen with line (1 or 2) and the envelope chosen with env (DCO pitch \, DCW wave \, DCA amplitude) \, in tone A or \, with edit B \, in tone B of a split or mix. The cells follow the selection. \; An envelope has 8 steps of rate and level. sus is the step that holds while the key is down (off: none) \, end the last step \, which goes to zero. Easy A D S R write a simple envelope into the selected one: attack to the top \, decay to the sustain level \, release to zero. \; PERFORM and SETUP (beige) are not stored. OPERATION (green) is the operation memory of the CZ-1: key mode (normal \, split \, mix) \, split point \, tone B \, volumes \, chorus \, portamento \, glide \, bend range \, wheel and aftertouch. It is stored in an operation slot \, not in the tone. \; TONE band. name: type a new name (16 characters \, _ for a space). factory N: a factory tone \, from the CZ banks (.syx) beside cz4~. user N: a user slot \, 0 to 63. reload: the same tone again \, edits dropped. init: a plain sawtooth. compare: hear the stored tone while it is on. store to N: chooses the user slot \, save tone stores the edited tone there and writes the user bank \, see Presets. load bank \, write bank: read or write the bank file without storing. send bank \, send tone: as SysEx to MIDI out. \; operation N recalls an operation slot \, store to N chooses one \, save operation stores the current operation there and writes the operation file \, init operation goes back to one tone. \; MIDI in: the receive channel \, 0 = all. out: the channel of the controller feedback and of SysEx. CZ program \, get from CZ \, send to CZ: talk to a real CZ with its handshake \, see SysEx., f 64;
#X obj 60 1138 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Launchkey 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1166 Launchkey: the Novation Launchkey Mini MK4 with the custom firmware maltepeter2000/launchkey_firmware \, set up the same for every instrument of bela-workstation (launchkey/README.md there). \; cz4cc 1: the controller layer. Encoders in mode Custom 1 send CC pages from 20 in rows of 8 on the keys channel \, every change made elsewhere goes back to them on the send channel (txchannel of cz4~) \, CC 3 asks for all values. \; cz4pads 10: the pads in Drum mode (notes 36-51 on channel 10 \, the Drums Channel): top row 36 factory + \, 37 user + \, 38 init (press twice within a second) \, 39-43 own \, bottom row 44 factory - \, 45 user - \, 46 save \, 47-51 own. cz4~ has no own pads yet. \; Storing asks first: save once shows Store to? and the user slot played or stored last (savearm) \, user + / - choose the slot (saveslot 1 / -1 \, nothing is recalled) \, save again stores there and writes the user bank (save). Any other pad or 10 s cancel (savecancel). Own pads and init after its first press show what they do on the display. \; Pad colours \, sent by cz4pads itself with noteout on channel 10 (velocity = colour + 32 x mode): factory blue \, user and save green (the user bank) \, init orange (flashing while the second press is awaited) \, save flashing while it asks and white for a moment when stored \, own pads purple \, free pads dark. They go out at load \, on leds \, and when the Launchkey asks for them (CC 3 = 127 on channel 10 \, sent when Drum mode is selected). \; lkdisplay: the display lines (display <title> <value>: the control you turn \, Preset \, User \, Init or Stored with the patch name) as SysEx for the Launchkey's display -> midiout., f 64;
#X obj 60 1644 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Inlet 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1672 1 float: note number \, velocity 100. \; 1 list: note \, velocity and \, if you like \, the MIDI channel. \; 1 anything: a message \, see Messages., f 64;
#X obj 60 1734 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Outlets 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1762 1 signal: left output. \; 2 signal: right output. \; 3 anything: info \, name \, 0-127 and value text for every \;   change \, the tones that play \, their names \, the channels \, \;   display lines., f 64;
#X obj 60 1856 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Presets\ and\ user\ bank 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 1884 preset selects a factory tone \, user a slot of the user bank. They go to the tone chosen with edit: A \, or B of a split or mix. The third outlet answers with tonea or toneb \, the bank \, the number and the name. \; The user bank (64 tones \, cz4user-bank.syx) and the operation memory (cz4user-op.syx) are files in the folder of your patch \, so every project keeps its own. cz4.i~ reads them at load if they are there \, otherwise the files beside cz4~ are the starting point. save \, userwrite \, userread \, opwrite and opread without a file name use them: store to N in the editor chooses the slot \, save tone stores and writes. Save the patch first \, an unsaved patch has no folder of its own. \; There is one user bank and one operation memory in Pd \, not one per object: two cz4.i~ in one patch share them. \; op recalls an operation slot: key mode \, split point \, tone B and the rest of the OPERATION rows. Tone B is loaded from its bank and number., f 64;
#X obj 60 2170 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Messages 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2198 name v: set a control \, in the values the CZ shows. \; name: report it as info. \; n name v: set it from a pot or a MIDI CC \, 0 to 127. \; ninfo name: report it as info. \; line 1/2 \, env 0-2 \, edit 0/1: what the line \, envelope \, rate \;   and level controls work on (DCO DCW DCA \, tone A or B). \; preset n: a factory tone \, read only. \; user n: a slot of the user bank \, 0 to 63. \; init: a plain sawtooth tone to start from. \; reload: the same tone again \, edits dropped. \; compare 0/1: hear the stored tone instead of the edit. \; store n: the edited tone into user slot n \, in memory. \;   Without n: the user slot played or stored last. \; save: store \, then write the user bank (the pads' save). \; savearm \, saveslot n \, savecancel: the pads' store with a \;   question: show the slot \, move it \, drop it. save after \;   savearm stores into the slot shown. \; presetstep [n] \, userstep [n]: the factory tone or user \;   slot n after the one played last \, wrapping (the pads). \; name text: rename the edited tone (16 characters). \; copyline 1 2: line 1 into line 2 (or 2 1). \; copyenv 1 DCW 2 DCW: one envelope into another. \; userwrite [file] \, userread [file]: the user bank \, see \;   Presets. A file name without a path is beside cz4~. \; usersend: the user bank as SysEx. \; presets \, users: list the names. \; op n: recall operation slot n \, opstore n: store it \, \;   opinit: back to one tone \, opwrite [file] \, opread [file]: \;   the operation memory \, see Presets. ops: the used slots. \; sysex bytes: one SysEx message from a list. sysexdump: \;   the edited tone as SysEx. czget p \, czsend p \, czmodel 1/101: \;   see SysEx. \; bend f: pitch wheel \, -1 to 1 \, times bendrange. \; mod f: modulation wheel \, 0 to 1: vibrato. \; at f: aftertouch \, 0 to 1. \; sustain 0/1: hold pedal. \; channel n: MIDI receive channel \, 0 is all. \; txchannel n: channel of the controller feedback and of \;   SysEx \, 1 to 16. \; status: report tones \, operation slot \, channels \, voices. \; stop: all notes off (they release). \; reset: silence at once., f 64;
#X obj 60 2884 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty The\ instrument 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 2912 A tone is a CZ tone: two lines \, each with a wave pair and a window \, and three envelopes per line with 8 steps each: DCO (pitch) \, DCW (the phase distortion \, which does what a filter does on other synthesizers) and DCA (amplitude). Line select plays line 1 \, line 2 \, line 1 twice with line 2 detuned (1+1') or both (1+2'). Line 2 can be ring-modulated by line 1 or have its pitch thrown about by noise. \; Every voice has its own six envelopes: the instrument is fully polyphonic. As on the CZ there are 8 lines: 8 notes of a one-line tone \, 4 of a two-line tone (voices raises this up to 16). \; From the CZ-1: 144-byte tones with line levels and velocity on each envelope \, names \, the operation memory with split and tone mix of two tones \, portamento \, glide \, bend range \, wheel and aftertouch \, and the chorus. The waves are those of the uPD933 chip as MAME models it \, computed with the chip's 12-bit tables (chip 0 gives ideal ones). \; From Arturia's CZ V the idea of simpler access: the PERFORM row changes brightness \, attack \, release \, balance and detune of the playing tone without touching it \, and the easy envelope writes a whole 8-step envelope from four values. Everything stays a CZ tone \, so it can go to a CZ and back. \; Timings the chip does not fix (vibrato clock \, velocity and key follow curves \, portamento \, glide \, chorus) are estimates for now., f 64;
#X obj 60 3326 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty SysEx 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 3354 The object speaks the exclusive format of the CZ series. A tone travels as nibbles \, the low one first: 256 for the 128 bytes of a CZ-101 \, 1000 \, 3000 or 5000 \, 288 for the 144 bytes of a CZ-1. The bytes arrive with the rest of the MIDI at MIDI in and leave MIDI out. \; As a device it answers like a CZ \, with Casio's handshake: a send request (F0 44 00 00 7n 10 or 11 \, program) and a receive request (20 or 21) are answered with F0 44 00 00 7n 30 \, and the tone follows. So CZ editors and librarians work with it. Program 96 (hex 60) is the tone A that plays \, 32 to 95 the user slots 0 to 63 \, 0 to 31 the first factory tones. \; As a host it talks to a real CZ: czget p asks it for program p \, czsend p sends it the edited tone. czmodel 101 makes both use the 128-byte format of the CZ-101 family \, czmodel 1 (default) the CZ-1's. \; sysexdump sends the edited tone and usersend the 64 tones of the user bank as librarian messages (receive request with the data in the same message). Such messages and .syx files of librarians are taken at MIDI in or with sysex b b b., f 64;
#X obj 60 3672 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Data\ files 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 3700 The object needs no files. Without them the factory bank holds the INIT tone. \; Every .syx file in the folder of cz4~ is read for CZ tones (CZ-101 \, 1000 \, 3000 \, 5000 with 128 bytes \, CZ-1 with 144) and they join the factory bank in alphabetical order of the files. Casio's own tones are not part of this project: put your own dumps there. \; cz4user-bank.syx beside cz4~ is a user bank: 64 CZ-1 tones as a librarian keeps them \, so other CZ tools read it as well. cz4user-op.syx holds operation memory: a message of its own per used slot (F0 7D \, the ID for non-commercial use). For cz4.i~ they are the starting point \, see Presets. \; For cz4.i~: cz4~ and cz4.i~.pd in a folder on Pd's search path., f 64;
#X obj 60 3938 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty Controls 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 3966 In the order of the editor: one heading per row \, the same title as the row there \, page k on the controller is row k. Each line: name (the label in the editor) \, range \, CC number and what it does. The line \, envelope \, rate and level controls act on the selection (line \, env \, edit)., f 64;
#X obj 60 4060 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty PAGE\ 1\ \ PERFORM\ \ CC\ 20-27 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 4088 dcw (DCW offset) -64..63 \, CC 20: brighter or darker: added to \;   the DCW of both lines \; detune (Detune L2) -64..63 \, CC 21: line 2 against line 1 \, in \;   cents \, on top of the tone \; attack (Attack) -64..63 \, CC 22: faster (-) or slower (+) steps \;   up to the sustain point of every envelope \; release (Release) -64..63 \, CC 23: faster (-) or slower (+) \;   steps after the sustain point \; vibrato (Vibrato) 0..99 \, CC 24: extra vibrato depth \, as the \;   mod wheel \; chorus (Chorus mix) 0..127 \, CC 25: level of the chorus for \;   tones with chorus on \; balance (Balance) -64..63 \, CC 26: line 1 (-) against line 2 \;   (+) \; volume (Volume) 0..127 \, CC 27: master volume, f 64;
#X obj 60 4342 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty PAGE\ 2\ \ LINE\ /\ WAVE\ \ CC\ 28\ 29\ 30\ 31\ 33\ 34\ 35\ 36 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 4370 line (Edit line) 0..1 \, CC 28: the line that the line and \;   envelope controls edit \; linesel (Line select) 0..3 \, CC 29: line 1 \, line 2 \, line 1 \;   twice (line 2 detuned) \, both lines \; wave (Wave) 0..7 \, CC 30: first wave of the line \; wave2 (Wave 2) 0..8 \, CC 31: second wave: the line alternates \;   the two every cycle \; window (Window) 0..7 \, CC 33: window of the resonance waves (CZ \;   waves 6 \, 7 \, 8 = saw \, tri \, trap) \; ringmod (Modulation) 0..2 \, CC 34: line 2 ring-modulated by \;   line 1 \, or its pitch by noise (1+1' and 1+2') \; octave (Octave) -1..1 \, CC 35: octave of the tone \; level (Line level) 1..15 \, CC 36: level of the line (CZ-1), f 64;
#X obj 60 4592 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty PAGE\ 3\ \ DETUNE\ /\ VIBRATO\ \ CC\ 37\ 39\ 40\ 41\ 42\ 43\ 44\ 45 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 4620 dsign (Det. sign) 0..1 \, CC 37: detune of line 2 up or down \; doct (Det. octave) 0..3 \, CC 39: detune of line 2 in octaves \; dnote (Det. note) 0..11 \, CC 40: detune of line 2 in semitones \; dfine (Det. fine) 0..60 \, CC 41: fine detune of line 2 \, 60 = \;   one semitone \; vwave (Vib. wave) 0..3 \, CC 42: vibrato wave \; vdelay (Vib. delay) 0..99 \, CC 43: time until the vibrato sets \;   in \; vrate (Vib. rate) 0..99 \, CC 44: vibrato speed \; vdepth (Vib. depth) 0..99 \, CC 45: vibrato depth, f 64;
#X obj 60 4794 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty PAGE\ 4\ \ ENVELOPE\ \ CC\ 46-53 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 4822 env (Edit env) 0..2 \, CC 46: the envelope that the rate \, level \, \;   sus and end controls edit: pitch \, wave \, amplitude \; sus (Sustain) 0..8 \, CC 47: step that holds while the key is \;   down \, the steps after it are the release \; end (End) 1..8 \, CC 48: last step: it goes to zero \; kfw (Key DCW) 0..9 \, CC 49: key follow of the DCW: high notes \;   get less \; kfa (Key DCA) 0..9 \, CC 50: key follow of the DCA: high notes \;   get faster \; velp (Velo pitch) 0..15 \, CC 51: velocity to the DCO envelope \;   (CZ-1) \; velw (Velo DCW) 0..15 \, CC 52: velocity to the DCW envelope \;   (CZ-1) \; vela (Velo DCA) 0..15 \, CC 53: velocity to the amplitude (CZ-1), f 64;
#X obj 60 5060 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty PAGE\ 5\ \ RATES\ \ CC\ 54-61 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 5088 r1 (Rate 1) 0..99 \, CC 54: rate of step 1: 99 fastest \; r2 (Rate 2) 0..99 \, CC 55: rate of step 2: 99 fastest \; r3 (Rate 3) 0..99 \, CC 56: rate of step 3: 99 fastest \; r4 (Rate 4) 0..99 \, CC 57: rate of step 4: 99 fastest \; r5 (Rate 5) 0..99 \, CC 58: rate of step 5: 99 fastest \; r6 (Rate 6) 0..99 \, CC 59: rate of step 6: 99 fastest \; r7 (Rate 7) 0..99 \, CC 60: rate of step 7: 99 fastest \; r8 (Rate 8) 0..99 \, CC 61: rate of step 8: 99 fastest, f 64;
#X obj 60 5230 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty PAGE\ 6\ \ LEVELS\ \ CC\ 62\ 63\ 70\ 71\ 72\ 73\ 74\ 75 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 5258 l1 (Level 1) 0..99 \, CC 62: level of step 1 \; l2 (Level 2) 0..99 \, CC 63: level of step 2 \; l3 (Level 3) 0..99 \, CC 70: level of step 3 \; l4 (Level 4) 0..99 \, CC 71: level of step 4 \; l5 (Level 5) 0..99 \, CC 72: level of step 5 \; l6 (Level 6) 0..99 \, CC 73: level of step 6 \; l7 (Level 7) 0..99 \, CC 74: level of step 7 \; l8 (Level 8) 0..99 \, CC 75: level of step 8, f 64;
#X obj 60 5400 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty PAGE\ 7\ \ EASY\ ENV\ /\ TOUCH\ \ CC\ 76-83 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 5428 eattack (Easy A) 0..99 \, CC 76: easy envelope: attack time. \;   Writes steps 1-3 of the selected envelope \; edecay (Easy D) 0..99 \, CC 77: easy envelope: decay time \; esustain (Easy S) 0..99 \, CC 78: easy envelope: sustain level \; erelease (Easy R) 0..99 \, CC 79: easy envelope: release time \; edit (Edit tone) 0..1 \, CC 80: the tone that the edit controls \;   work on: A \, or B of a split or mix \; wheel (Wheel vib.) 0..99 \, CC 81: vibrato depth of the mod \;   wheel \; atvib (AT vibrato) 0..99 \, CC 82: aftertouch to vibrato depth \; atamp (AT amp) 0..15 \, CC 83: aftertouch to amplitude, f 64;
#X obj 60 5618 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty PAGE\ 8\ \ OPERATION\ \ CC\ 85\ 86\ 87\ 89\ 90\ 91\ 92\ 93 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 5646 keymode (Key mode) 0..2 \, CC 85: tone A alone \, A above and B \;   below the split point \, or A and B on every key \; split (Split) 0..127 \, CC 86: split point: the lowest key of \;   tone A \; bsrc (B bank) 0..1 \, CC 87: bank of tone B \; bnum (B number) 0..127 \, CC 89: tone B: its number in that bank \; avol (A volume) 0..99 \, CC 90: volume of tone A \; bvol (B volume) 0..99 \, CC 91: volume of tone B \; boct (B octave) -2..2 \, CC 92: octave of tone B \; bdet (B detune) -64..63 \, CC 93: detune of tone B in cents \;   (mix), f 64;
#X obj 60 5836 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty PAGE\ 9\ \ OPERATION\ 2\ \ CC\ 94\ 95\ 102\ 103\ 104\ 105\ 106\ 107 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 5864 achorus (A chorus) 0..1 \, CC 94: chorus for tone A \; bchorus (B chorus) 0..1 \, CC 95: chorus for tone B \; porta (Portamento) 0..1 \, CC 102: notes slide from the last one \; ptime (Porta time) 0..99 \, CC 103: portamento time \; glide (Glide) 0..1 \, CC 104: every note starts at gnote and \;   slides in \; gnote (Glide note) -24..24 \, CC 105: start of the glide \, in \;   semitones from the key \; gtime (Glide time) 0..99 \, CC 106: glide time \; solo (Solo) 0..1 \, CC 107: one voice \, the last key. Legato \;   keeps the envelopes, f 64;
#X obj 60 6054 cnv 10 10 10 empty empty PAGE\ 10\ \ SETUP\ \ CC\ 108-112 24 6 0 14 #1e3791 #000000 0;
#X text 82 6082 bendrange (Bend range) 0..12 \, CC 108: pitch bend range in \;   semitones \; voices (Voices) 1..16 \, CC 109: notes of a one-line tone (the \;   CZ: 8) \, a two-line tone plays half as many \; tune (Tune) -64..63 \, CC 110: master tune in cents \; transpose (Transpose) -24..24 \, CC 111: transposition in \;   semitones \; chip (Waves) 0..1 \, CC 112: chip: the waves as the CZ's chip \;   computes them (12-bit) \, clean: ideal, f 64;
#X text 82 6246 Credits: uPD933 model by Devin Acker (MAME) \, CZ engine after melodee by Kerem Kilic (BSD-3)\; CZ tone format after Casio's MIDI specifications\; cz4~ by Peter with help by Claude, f 64;
#X connect 5 0 7 0;
#X connect 5 1 7 1;
